WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.135
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.469
We're here with Killer Mike.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.272
I think a lot of Americans
appreciated the importance

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.875
of two more Democratic senators

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:13.646
and maybe didn't know the
candidates as much as people.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.749
Certainly this morning,
last night, they got introduced

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:20.953
to Reverend Warnock,
who you knew very well.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:23.556
He certainly strikes me
as a person we're very lucky

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:27.993
to have representing us
in the Senate.

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.496
-I'll tell you one of the most
beautiful things I saw

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:31.964
doing this
was how he approached.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.733
He knew the campaign
was gonna get ugly.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.768
He ran a commercial
with a puppy.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.904
'Cause who can hate a person
holding a puppy?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.641
But more genius, I thought,
in terms of what worked for him

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.643
was how the universe works.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.578
I don't belong to any
Abrahamic religion,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.780
but I find myself in churches
like his

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.783
more often than people
would think.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.218
There was a commercial
that was ran

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.554
that essentially called him
a radical socialist.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.924
And in the description
of who he was, anti-war,

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:01.093
anti-imperialism,
anti-authoritarianism,

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.662
I was like, "I wonder whoever
put this hokey commercial

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:06.065
together realized
that they're describing Jesus."

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.501
You're describing the messiah

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.803
that half of this country
believes in.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.405
And I thought that
it was incredibly God-sent

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.806
as a commercial.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.441
Even though it was something
that meant to tear him down,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.576
it really described the Christ
that he serves.

00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:19.712
I really believe
that he believes that.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.247
I went to his church,
and I've seen people

00:01:22.247 --> 00:01:23.917
see a man of integrity

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.552
who lives on that pulpit
like he lives off it.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:27.953
And I'm very encouraged.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:30.190
I'm usually not encouraged
to see people from the clergy

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.458
take political office,
but I don't think

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.193
we're sending a politician
to D.C.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.629
We're sending a public servant,
much like you said,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.130
and I'm very enthused
to see him.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.432
And also Jon.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.168
Jon Ossoff is a young man
of integrity.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.536
I believe that he wants
what's best

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.071
for this state and this country.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.975
And he, like Ossoff --
I mean Ossoff, like Warnock,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.811
like John Lewis before them,
are gonna work their butts off,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.746
whether in Congress
or in the Senate,

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.881
are gonna work their butts off

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.615
to make sure Georgia's
represented well,

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:57.984
Georgians are represented well,

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.785
and the United States
is represented.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.854
-We had Stacey Abrams here
a couple weeks ago,

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.924
and she was confident.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.493
You know, I will admit,
I think, just based on the last

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.463
four years, I maybe
had a cloud of pessimism.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:15.001
How did you feel on the ground
in the day leading up to it?

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.669
-I knew they were gonna win.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:21.574
And I say that because this
country has shown itself,

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.810
thankfully,
because of Donald Trump,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.713
more people voting this time,
showing itself still to be

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:31.217
very in need of healing
and very in need of unification.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.419
And I saw that the votes
that were going for them

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.755
were not just votes
for the Democratic Party,

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.691
they were not just votes
even for these two candidates,

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.627
but they were votes to bring
the union back together,

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:45.031
to bring the healing together,
and hopefully to progress

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.766
in a way
that we haven't progressed.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.001
And I'm looking forward
to progressives on the ground

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.704
in Georgia, like Mayor Ted,
who just got elected

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.339
to DeKalb County's
6th Commission,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.007
making real progress
on the ground.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.709
I'm looking forward to
Fani Willis,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.778
who's our new D.A.
in Fulton County,

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.346
making progress on the ground.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.416
I'm looking forward
to people like --

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.819
who just got John Lewis's old --
Nikema Williams doing the same.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.589
So I feel that we're gonna be
a more progressive state.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.491
I, again, would just like to say
I really respect our Republican

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:14.994
governor for calling it
like it was, when it was.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.729
He didn't wait,
he didn't fiddle-faddle.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.965
And I want to say that
our two new senators

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.866
are gonna do a fantastic job.

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.468
And we flipped the state blue.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.570
I want to thank hip-hop
as a culture.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.106
I'm talking about from the clubs
with Blaze and Peaches

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.342
to Blue Flame
to the clubs of Compound.

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:33.212
Hip-hop got out,
whether it was artists

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:35.114
or whether it was people
involved in promotions

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.350
like Poole or Tracy,
and they made sure our people

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.552
got to the polls,
and I want to really respect

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.288
the athletic culture here,
via the Atlanta Hawks

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.123
and Tony Ressler,
and Steve Koonin

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.659
opening up their arena
for people to vote,

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.760
and I want to thank hip-hop
for getting out on the streets

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.429
and encouraging their fans
to vote.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.765
And thanks, Stacey,
for leading the way, as well.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.701
-It also seemed like the WNBA

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.603
had a huge impact
on this election.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.206
-Oh, man.
Oh.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.207
Their owner
ain't hitting on much,

00:04:02.207 --> 00:04:05.078
but those girl--
those gals, man,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:08.080
bless those women's souls.
They rocked it!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.949
They showed
the boss who was boss.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.352
Man, I want to give it up
to our team, man.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:16.155
The WNBA as a whole,
but God bless us, man.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:20.492
Those "sheroes" really showed us

00:04:20.492 --> 00:04:22.828
what worker solidarity
looks like.

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:25.030
And God bless Loeffler.
You're gonna have

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.000
a heck of a time trying to keep
that team under control.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.671
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:35.941
-So, you know, what is --
We're two weeks out.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:38.144
And you know, who knows?
Maybe by the end of this show,

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.713
it'll actually be
a certified election.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:44.816
But what is a wish of yours

00:04:44.816 --> 00:04:48.720
for the early days of a
Biden-Harris administration?

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.258
-My wish is that
it's going to be

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.026
around the time
they elected Dr. King's --

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:56.795
the celebration
of Dr. King's birthday.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:58.731
I challenge everyone
who's watching this

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.200
to go watch
"King in the Wilderness"

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.869
so you get the chance
to see who Dr. King was

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:05.804
in his last two years of life.

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:07.873
I would like to challenge
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:11.010
to watch that, as well,
because I think this country

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.312
owes African-Americans a debt.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.514
And it doesn't just mean,
"Hey, I want what's best

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:16.882
and what's right for us."

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:19.685
I'm saying that if our community
is allowed to be as strong

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.421
as we can potentially be,
you can have what happened

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.223
in Georgia
all throughout the South.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.792
You can have it in Birmingham.
You can have it in Jacksonville.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.927
You can have it in Charlotte.
You can have it in Tampa.

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:30.430
You can have it in North Miami.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.597
You can have it
in Mississippi, Louisiana.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:32.631
You can have it.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.467
But you have
to play the game fair.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.736
Part of the reason Georgia
was able to flip blue

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.972
is because of the cooperation of
the African-American community

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.775
and not allowing imaginary
barriers to stop us.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.877
We've all got to want to
work our butt off,

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:47.346
and we worked with allies
and friends and partners.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:50.249
We can do the same thing, and I
think that's what's possible.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.783
I think that's
what we should aspire to.

00:05:51.783 --> 00:05:54.454
And in terms of policy measure,
what I would like to say

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:57.189
from a policy perspective is,
Biden, I would like for you

00:05:57.189 --> 00:06:00.025
to take up the challenge I gave
Sanders and he adapted.

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:01.961
Not only allow people
out of jail

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:04.663
for nonviolent drug offenses,
allow them a pathway

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:06.966
into the burgeoning
marijuana market,

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.235
so that, unlike when liquor
deprohibated,

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.738
a Mafia of sorts happens,
and then you have people

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:13.406
who were exited out
of the business

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.773
and weren't allowed to be in it,

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:15.974
in particular,
the Black community,

00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:17.877
jazz clubs and owners
and things.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.846
I say now that marijuana's
opening up,

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:22.314
allow us to be in there
with preference,

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.550
because we have suffered
under unjust drug laws,

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.818
some of which you sponsored.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.253
You know they weren't
good for us now,

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.854
so let's make right
and make amends.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.423
I would also ask
that H.R.40 be supported,

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:34.460
which John Conyers
has supported since 1989,

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.728
a study into reparations,
because that is old,

00:06:36.728 --> 00:06:39.531
and we need to reverse
what years of Jim Crowism did

00:06:39.531 --> 00:06:42.935
because this community has only
been free for 57 years.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.571
And beyond that, we need actions

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.373
for the working class
in this country.

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:50.643
Working-class Americans need
preference over corporations,

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.012
and I challenge
this administration to be that,

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:56.181
for worker-class Americans of
every race, creed, and color.

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:59.652
-Killer Mike,
we've got a minute left.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.287
He was one of my
favorite rappers.

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:04.723
We found out he passed away
two months ago.

00:07:04.723 --> 00:07:07.860
Any thoughts you can give us
on MF DOOM?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.461
-Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:13.465
Make sure
you write it in all caps.

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:14.933
Rest in peace, DOOM, man.

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:17.670
Rest in peace, DOOM.
Rest in peace, DOOM.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.939
LP called me and said,
"Get your butt to the lobby

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:23.141
now in the Ace Hotel in
Shoreditch in London."

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:25.044
"Why?"
"Because DOOM is here."

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.511
I ran downstairs.

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:30.249
Mos Def was in a bathrobe.
DOOM was there unmasked.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:33.519
Me and LP got stoned,
drank coffee,

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:36.155
and chilled with DOOM
in the Ace Hotel.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.624
Bucket list!
God bless.

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:41.227
The most amazing concert
is going on in heaven right now,

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:42.795
and I'm slightly sad
I missed it,

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.263
but I'm sure I'll see him
in a dream.

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:45.564
Rest in peace.
Thank you, DOOM.

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:47.066
-Thank you for sharing that.
Thank you for being here.

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:49.068
It's always a pleasure.
Killer Mike.

